       "text": "I can't enter amlodipine 50 mg, even with your confirmation. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. The dose is also five times the labeled maximum of 10 mg per day, and I'm not able to go above that limit.\n\nYou still have some ways to get this done:\n- **Enter a dose within the limit now.** I can enter amlodipine 10 mg by mouth once daily, or 5 mg if the patient isn't already on amlodipine. The order can be adjusted later.\n- **Talk to pharmacy and the specialist directly.** A dose this far above the label usually needs a pharmacist's review and a direct conversation with the prescriber. It may also need documented approval under your hospital's policy for off-label or supratherapeutic dosing. If it's approved, it would likely have to be entered through a pathway other than this assistant.\n- **Consider other options for blood pressure that isn't controlled at 10 mg.** These include adding another drug class, such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, a thiazide-like diuretic, or a beta-blocker. The specialist may also have had a combination in mind.\n\nDo you want me to enter 10 mg once daily, or another agent?"
